{
  "$schema": "https://go.kicad.org/pcm/schemas/v1",
  "name": "Via Stitching",
  "description": "Stitch copper zones together with a grid of vias on a chosen net",
  "description_full": "Fills the overlap of a net's copper zones (for example the top and bottom GND pours) with a grid of stitching vias, on whichever two copper layers you pick.\n\nWorks on KiCad 6 and later. There are two builds, and the Plugin and Content Manager installs whichever one your KiCad runs.\n\nFeatures:\n- Through, Micro, Blind, Buried, and Blind/Buried via types, on any layer pair.\n- Hexagonal, square, or staggered patterns, with configurable diameter, drill, and spacing.\n- X/Y offset for stitching more than one pattern onto the same area without overlap.\n- Automatically avoids other nets' tracks, pads, zones, and existing holes, with proper clearances.\n- Select an existing via to clone its settings, or let the dialog remember your last run.\n- Placed vias are grouped together, and Reset last run deletes a whole run as a set.\n- Dialog follows KiCad's own configured UI language: English, Dutch, German, or French.",
